    <p class="statement"><strong>Graduate education participates in imagining what an academic is supposed to look like.</strong></p>
    <p class="citation">(Ellsworth 6, 47)</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="daemon" class="screen" data-note="SCREEN 6 — THE DAEMON. This is the hinge. Mad has been hanging around the talk. Take Zweig's positive unrest carefully, name peril, and say listening is not obedience.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tone" style="background:var(--skin-5)"></span>THE HINGE · THE DAEMON</div>
    <div class="daemon-stage">
      <div>
        <h2>the unrest<br>that is in us all.</h2>
        <div class="poetic-lines">
          <p>the question that will not leave</p>
          <p class="indent">the connection that follows me home</p>
          <p>the sentence that arrives</p>
          <p class="indent">before I know why it belongs</p>
          <p class="whisper">the feeling that the argument is not yet finished</p>
        </div>
        <p class="statement"><strong>Listening is not obedience.</strong><br>Compliance is not the same thing as learning.</p>
        <p class="citation">(Zweig 243–45)</p>
      </div>
</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="conduction" class="screen" data-note="SCREEN 7 — CONDUCTION. Change scale from BIG MOVEMENTS to LITTLE MOVEMENTS. Use Zweig's lightning-conductor image carefully and ask your central mentorship question.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tone" style="background:var(--skin-3)"></span>THE TURN · CONDUCTION</div>
    <h2>not replication.<br>not abandonment.<br><em>conduction.</em></h2>
    <p class="lede">Writing about Hölderlin, Zweig describes the poet as a “lightning-conductor” who receives an overwhelming force and passes it into form (289–90).</p>
    <p class="statement"><strong>How do we help students conduct overwhelming intellectual, creative, ethical, and affective energies into forms that can sustain a life of inquiry—or even just the moment of graduate school?</strong></p>
    <div class="turnline"></div>
    <div class="big-movements"><span>institutional routes</span><span>overlapping thresholds</span><span>unequal recognition</span><span>institutional time</span><span>recognizable state</span></div>
    <div class="poetic-lines"><p>What I have instead are</p><p class="indent"><strong>little movements.</strong></p><p class="whisper">not remedies / not a universal model / smaller orientations that might make room</p></div>
    <p class="citation">(Zweig 289–90)</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="notice" class="screen little-screen" data-note="SCREEN 8 — NOTICE. Ram Dass: intellect as exquisite tool; movement from intellect to intuition; witness notices before judging. Keep this brief and spacious.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="little-sub">LITTLE MOVEMENT 1 · INTUITION + WITNESSING</div>
    <div class="little-word">NOTICE</div>
    <p class="little-thesis">Notice before immediately judging.</p>
    <div class="echo-field" aria-label="Recurring questions">
      <span>there is that question again.</span><span>that source keeps bothering me.</span><span>something here does not fit.</span><span>I don't know what this means yet.</span><span class="witness-word">witness</span>
    </div>
    <p class="statement">Not everything we notice will become scholarship.<br><strong>But we cannot examine what we have trained ourselves not to hear.</strong></p>
    <p class="citation">(Dass 75, 80)</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="wait" class="screen little-screen" data-note="SCREEN 9 — WAIT. Active waiting and serendipity. Goggin and Goggin; Koupf; Wetherbee Phelps. Land on Proceed as way opens.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="little-sub">LITTLE MOVEMENT 2 · ACTIVE WAITING + SERENDIPITY</div>
    <div class="little-word">WAIT</div>
    <p class="little-thesis">Remain open while continuing to do the work.</p>
    <div class="wait-field" aria-hidden="true"><div class="wait-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div>
    <div class="poetic-lines">
      <p>not sit and wait for magic.</p>
      <p>not force the route.</p>
      <p class="indent"><strong>Proceed.</strong></p>
      <p class="deep"><strong>As way opens.</strong></p>
    </div>
    <p class="citation">(Goggin and Goggin 4; Koupf 54–55; Phelps 2)</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="accompany" class="screen little-screen" data-note="SCREEN 10 — ACCOMPANY. Intellectual companionship + presence. Godbee's relational response and feminist co-mentoring as power with.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="little-sub">LITTLE MOVEMENT 3 · INTELLECTUAL COMPANIONSHIP + PRESENCE</div>
    <div class="little-word">ACCOMPANY</div>
    <p class="little-thesis">Do not make graduate students inhabit uncertainty alone.</p>
    <div class="accompany">
      <div class="side"><h3>power over</h3><p>Here is what I did.<br>Become that.</p></div>
      <div class="bridge">→</div>
      <div class="side power-with"><h3>power with</h3><div class="presence-lines"><p>I am here.</p><p>Show me what you are seeing.</p><p>You do not have to know all of it yet.</p><p>What would help us test this?</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="citation">(Godbee 44–48)</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="mark" class="screen little-screen" data-note="SCREEN 11 — MARK. Little rituals. Recognize movement before graduation; not more assignments or labor. Give examples quickly.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="little-sub">LITTLE MOVEMENT 4 · LITTLE RITUALS</div>
    <div class="little-word">MARK</div>
    <p class="little-thesis">Recognize movement before graduation.</p>
    <div class="ritual-route" aria-label="Small moments worth marking">
      <div class="mark" style="--tone:var(--skin-1)">an argument abandoned</div>
      <div class="mark" style="--tone:var(--skin-2)">a rejection / resubmission</div>
      <div class="mark" style="--tone:var(--skin-3)">a return after leave</div>
      <div class="mark" style="--tone:var(--skin-4)">a changed method</div>
      <div class="mark" style="--tone:var(--skin-5)">a chapter that took longer</div>
      <div class="mark" style="--tone:var(--gray-2)">a dissertation becoming another dissertation</div>
    </div>
    <div class="poetic-lines"><p>Sometimes the little ritual simply says:</p><p class="indent"><strong>Something changed here.</strong></p><p class="deep">And that counts.</p></div>
    <p class="citation">(Pinkert and Bowen 16, 27–36; Phelps 14)</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="care" class="screen little-screen" data-note="SCREEN 12 — CARE. Care + hope. Do not individualize self-care. Make intellectual risk materially possible.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="little-sub">LITTLE MOVEMENT 5 · CARE + HOPE</div>
    <div class="little-word">CARE</div>
    <p class="little-thesis">Make intellectual risk materially possible.</p>
    <div class="care-stage">
      <div class="commands"><h3>care as assignment</h3><ul><li>practice self-care</li><li>set better boundaries</li><li>be resilient</li></ul></div>
      <div class="material"><h3>care with material form</h3><ul><li>funding</li><li>healthcare</li><li>time</li><li>flexibility</li><li>food and rest</li><li>accessible spaces</li><li>reasonable workloads</li><li>someone who notices when the system becomes impossible</li></ul></div>
    </div>
    <p class="care-question"><strong>What would make this possible?</strong></p>
    <p class="small">instead of: Why can't you do this the way everyone else does?</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="allow" class="screen little-screen" data-note="SCREEN 13 — ALLOW. Unfinishedness. The smallest movement: stop treating unfinishedness as deficiency. Land on finishing requirement vs person.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="little-sub">LITTLE MOVEMENT 6 · UNFINISHEDNESS</div>
    <div class="little-word">ALLOW</div>
    <p class="little-thesis">Maybe the smallest movement is to stop treating unfinishedness as deficiency.</p>
    <div class="allow-list">
      <span style="--tone:var(--skin-1)">a mentor still changes</span><span style="--tone:var(--skin-2)">a professor becomes a novice</span><span style="--tone:var(--skin-3)">a dissertation ends without finishing the question</span><span style="--tone:var(--skin-4)">a career moves sideways</span><span style="--tone:var(--skin-5)">someone leaves</span><span style="--tone:var(--gray-2)">someone returns</span><span style="--tone:var(--skin-3)">someone becomes something nobody predicted</span>
    </div>
    <p class="bigline"><strong>Do not confuse finishing a requirement<br>with finishing a person.</strong></p>
    <p class="citation">(Phelps 14; Pinkert and Bowen 16, 27–36; Teeuwsen et al. 684)</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="poem" class="screen" data-note="SCREEN 14 — THE POEM. Reveal the performance as graduate-student performance-as-presentation. Pause and let the collective poem assemble. You can shuffle once, then freeze.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tone" style="background:var(--skin-2)"></span>THE PERFORMANCE · THE POEM</div>
    <div class="performance-reveal">
      <div class="meta">
        <h2>This version<br>did not exist<br>before this room.</h2>
        <p>Your words entered the route.</p><p>They crossed the timeline.</p><p>They resisted categories.</p><p>They encountered other people's words.</p>
        <p class="citation">Invention can emerge through a “mix of agencies” where chance, history, materials, environments, other people, and intentional action meet (Koupf 55).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="poem-shell">
        <div class="poem-controls"><span>room <code id="poem-room">rmmla2026</code></span><div><button id="shuffle-poem">rearrange</button><button id="freeze-poem">freeze</button><button id="export-poem">export</button></div></div>
        <div class="poem-output" id="poem-output" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="cycle-status" id="poem-page-status"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="statement">This poem cannot be exactly repeated because this room cannot be exactly repeated.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="becoming" class="screen" data-note="SCREEN 15 — BECOMING. Deliver the closing slowly. After the final sentence, stop speaking and press L once. Do not advance to a thank-you slide.">
  <div class="screen-inner">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tone" style="background:var(--skin-5)"></span>BECOMING</div>
    <div class="final-lines">
      <p>The student is moving.</p>
      <p>The discipline is moving.</p>
      <p>The institution is moving.</p>
      <p>The material conditions are moving.</p>
      <p>The imagined destination is moving too.</p>
      <br>
      <p>The route may be mapped.</p>
      <p>The journey cannot be predetermined.</p>
      <p class="final"><strong>Becoming cannot be predetermined.</strong></p>
    </div>
    <div class="unfinished" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>

